---
import Legend from './Legend.astro';
import Slider from './Slider.astro';
---

<figure class="kf-widget" data-kf-average>
  <div class="kf-widget__head">
    <span class="kf-widget__title">Moving average, level flight then a climb</span>
    <Legend items={[{ label: 'True altitude', tone: 'truth' }, { label: 'Reading', tone: 'reading', shape: 'dot' }, { label: 'Average', tone: 'estimate' }]} />
  </div>
  <div class="kf-plot" id="average-plot" data-plot data-label="Moving average of altimeter readings against the true altitude"></div>
  <div class="kf-controls">
    <Slider id="average-alpha" name="alpha" label="Blend factor α" min={0.02} max={1} step={0.01} value={0.1} />
  </div>
  <dl class="kf-stats">
    <div><dt>Noise left in level flight</dt><dd data-stat="noise"></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Lag while climbing</dt><dd data-stat="lag"></dd></div>
  </dl>
  <figcaption class="kf-caption">
    Slide α towards 0 and the line goes smooth, but it falls behind once the climb starts. Slide it towards 1 and it keeps up, but it jitters as much as the raw readings. No single α gives you both.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
  import { mountAverage } from '../scripts/average';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-kf-average]').forEach(mountAverage);
</script>
